LIKEOS-INSTALLER(1)          System Administration         LIKEOS-INSTALLER(1)

NAME
       likeos-installer - LikeOS Setup, the graphical installer

SYNOPSIS
       likeos-installer    [--mock]    [--window]   [--page=n   [--substep=n]]
       [--size=wxh] [--fast] [--no-animation]
       likeos-installer --version

DESCRIPTION
       likeos-installer is LikeOS Setup: the program that installs LikeOS from
       the USB medium onto a disk of the computer.  It is normally not started
       by hand.  The boot menu of the installation medium has an entry Install
       LikeOS from USB; it starts the medium's system with likeos.mode=install
       on the kernel command line, and init(8) then starts LikeOS Setup on the
       console instead of the login prompt: the X  server  with  this  program
       alone, full screen, without a window manager or desktop.

       Setup  asks,  page  by  page: the language and the formats of dates and
       times, the keyboard to use during setup, where LikeOS goes (a  disk  to
       erase  completely, or a partition, with tools to delete, create, format
       and extend partitions -- nothing  is  written  until  the  installation
       starts),  the  time  zone,  the keyboard layouts of the new system, the
       computer's name, the root password and the account to sign in with.   A
       summary  shows  every  choice  before anything is changed; Install then
       partitions and formats, unpacks the system image, sets up the new  sys-
       tem, installs the boot loader and registers it with the firmware, show-
       ing the progress, and restarts the computer into the installed system.

       The  disks of the medium Setup was started from are shown but cannot be
       chosen.  When something goes wrong a page says what, with the installa-
       tion log.

       The work is done by the installer library that the text-mode installer,
       likeos-install(1), uses too.  When the graphical installer  cannot  run
       (the  graphics  of the computer do not work), the installation medium's
       console offers likeos-install instead.

OPTIONS
       These are for developing and testing  Setup;  the  installation  medium
       starts it without any.

       --mock Use  the  built-in  stand-in  for the installer library: made-up
              disks and a simulated installation that changes nothing.

       --window
              Run in a normal 1024x768 window instead of covering the screen.

       --page=n
              Start on page n (0 the start screen, 1 language, 2  keyboard,  3
              preparing,  4  disk, 5 time zone, 6 keyboard layouts, 7 computer
              name, 8 root password, 9 account, 10 summary, 11 installing,  12
              finished,  13  error), with made-up answers for the pages before
              it -- for screenshots.

       --substep=n
              With --page: go n steps into a page that has steps.

       --size=wxh
              Lay the pages out as if the screen were wxh pixels.

       --fast No minimum time on the start and waiting screens.

       --no-animation
              Still illustrations and spinners.

       --version
              Show the version and exit.

EXIT STATUS
       0      The installation finished (Setup restarts the computer itself).

       10     The person chose to switch the computer off.

       other  Setup could not run or broke  down;  the  installation  medium's
              console then offers the text-mode installer.

FILES
       /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst
              The system image that is installed.

       /tmp/likeos-install.log
              The  log  of  the  installation (kept on the installed system as
              /var/log/likeos-install.log).

       /etc/inittab.install
              What  init(8)  runs   when   the   medium   was   started   with
              likeos.mode=install.

SEE ALSO
       likeos-install(1),   likeos-install.conf(5),   likeos-bootmenu.conf(5),
